  "facts": [
    "Bhumibol Bridge, a double cable‑stayed marvel, opened to traffic on 20 September 2006, beating its own official opening date of 5 December 2006 and instantly becoming Bangkok’s fastest link to Samut Prakan.",
    "Each of the bridge’s two 702‑meter and 582‑meter spans is supported by diamond‑shaped pylons towering 173 m and 164 m, while a free‑flowing interchange rises 50 m above the river where the spans meet.",
    "Named after King Bhumibol Adulyadej in 2009, the Bhumibol Bridge earned the nickname “Mega Bridge” and was spotlighted on the Discovery Channel, yet motorcycles were banned in 2018 for safety reasons."
  ],
